  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\quad A=\\{1,2, \\ldots, 11\\}$\r\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\\therefore & n(A)=11 \\text { and } B=\\{1,2, \\ldots, 10\\} \\\\ \\therefore & n(B)=10\\end{array}$\r\n$\\therefore \\text{Hence number of onto function}$ $=^{n(A)} C_{n(B)} \\times n(B) ! \\times n(B)$\r\n$={ }^{11} C_{10} \\times 10 ! \\times 10$\r\n$=(11 \\times 10 !) \\times 10=11 ! \\times 10$",
    "image": null
  },
